      "side": 0,
      "message": "Gah, good point. I tried to survey all the intervening code and found one issue.\n\nnotifyIfacesChangedForNetworkStats is using mNetworkAgentInfos to find the list of networks it has to update. This means, I think, that stats would not be updated correctly for a network that disconnects.\n\nIt sounds like the code is depending on the removal staying here then. I guess we should keep the remove() line here and have only the if (!contains) return; above. Really I\u0027d prefer the code to depend as little as possible on ordering of member mutation... But that\u0027s not something we can change immediately",
